      <ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 3500 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruk">Uruk</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> grows into the first city and the centre of the earliest known city-state</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">c. 2450 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eannatum">Eannatum of Lagash</a> records his victory over neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umma">Umma</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stele-of-the-vultures">Stele of the Vultures</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">338 BCE</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a> defeats <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece">Thebes</a> at Chaeronea and takes control of mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">562</span><span class="rf-text">Tikal is defeated by Caracol, an ally of Calakmul, in the wars of the Classic Maya city-states</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1176</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombard-league">Lombard League</a> of Italian communes defeats Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-legnano">Battle of Legnano</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1370</span><span class="rf-text">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stralsund">Stralsund</a> ends the Hanseatic towns’ war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> at the height of the league’s power</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1505</span><span class="rf-text">A Portuguese fleet sacks Kilwa and Mombasa, leading city-states of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> coast</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1965</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a> leaves the Federation of Malaysia and becomes an independent city-state</span></li></ol>
